  "question": {
    "text": "A conducting loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed perpendicular to a uniform magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. The magnetic field is decreased to zero in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> at a steady rate. The induced emf in the circular loop at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is:",
